## Step 5 — Update `src/services/documentAnalysisService.ts`

### 5a. Replace `supabase.auth.getSession()` (line ~156)
```ts
// BEFORE:
const { data: { session } } = await supabase.auth.getSession();
const token = session?.access_token;

// AFTER:
import { getStoredTokens } from '../lib/apiClient';
const { accessToken: token } = await getStoredTokens();
```

### 5b. Replace `supabase.functions.invoke('document-manager')` (line ~178)
```ts
// BEFORE:
const { data, error } = await supabase.functions.invoke('document-manager', { body: { ... } });

// AFTER:
const { data, error } = await functions.invoke('document-manager', { body: { ... } });
// Response shape is identical: { success, documentId, analysis, tokensUsed, duration, error, code }
```

### 5c. Replace RPC calls (lines ~229, ~266, ~291)
```ts
// BEFORE:
const { data } = await supabase.rpc('check_upload_limit', { p_user_id: userId, p_max_uploads: 5 });
const { data } = await supabase.rpc('increment_upload_count', { p_user_id: userId });
const { data } = await supabase.rpc('get_upload_count', { p_user_id: userId });

// AFTER:
const { data } = await rpc.call('check_upload_limit', { p_user_id: userId, p_max_uploads: 5 });
const { data } = await rpc.call('increment_upload_count', { p_user_id: userId });
const { data } = await rpc.call('get_upload_count', { p_user_id: userId });
```

