EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...

# Add:
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://api.dosiqai.com
```

### In `app.config.js` extra section:
```js
// Remove:
supabaseUrl: process.env.EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL,
supabaseAnonKey: process.env.EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY,

// Add:
apiBaseUrl: process.env.EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL,
```

---

## Step 14 — Remove Supabase package

```bash
npm uninstall @supabase/supabase-js react-native-url-polyfill
```

Remove the import from `supabaseClient.ts`:
```ts
// Remove this line:
import 'react-native-url-polyfill/auto';
```

---

## What Does NOT Need to Change

| Feature | Status |
|---|---|
| R2 Storage (`storageService.ts`) | ✅ Unchanged — R2 credentials and bucket are the same |
| UI components | ✅ Unchanged |
| Zustand store structure | ✅ Unchanged |
| Navigation (React Navigation) | ✅ Unchanged |
| AsyncStorage persistence | ✅ Unchanged — just different keys |
| Realtime subscriptions | ✅ N/A — none were used |
| Supabase Storage | ✅ N/A — app uses R2, not Supabase Storage |

---

## Important: Existing Users

All users from Supabase have been migrated to the VPS with their original UUIDs and bcrypt password hashes. **Existing users can log in with their original emails and passwords without any change.**

---

## Token Storage Keys

The new client uses these AsyncStorage keys (different from Supabase's internal keys — this clears any stale Supabase sessions automatically):
- `vps_access_token` — JWT access token
- `vps_refresh_token` — Refresh token
- `vps_user_data` — Cached user object JSON
